\pard\qc\sa80\f1\fs36\b\cf1 NeurIPS 2026 Reviewer Responses\b0\par
\pard\qc\sa240\f0\fs20\cf2 Submission 29735\par
\pard\sa60\f1\fs30\b\cf1 Reviewer QPha\b0\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp40\cf4\par
\pard\sb80\sa50\f0\fs17\b\cf2 ORIGINAL REVIEW\b0\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Official Review of Submission29735 by Reviewer QPha\line Official Reviewby Reviewer QPha26 Jun 2026, 07:51 (modified: 23 Jul 2026, 12:43)Program Chairs, Senior Area Chairs, Area Chairs, Reviewers Submitted, Authors, Reviewer QPhaRevisions\line Summary:\line This paper studies local credit assignment (LocalCA) in a tree-structured conductance-based model. The main insight of the paper is that for the considered tree-structured graph the gradient of the loss wrt to the local synaptic conductances factorises into a term that the authors call local eligibility (product of presynaptic activity, total input resistance of compartment, and the difference between the synaptic reversal potential and current compartment voltage (the driving force)) and a non-local compartment error. This compartment error is the somatic error scaled by a "path gain" through the tree. The authors propose that shunting inhibition multiplicatively modulates these path gains, which sometimes makes the exact error field more compressible and therefore easier to approximate with a low-bandwidth broadcast.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 The main contribution made by this submission is the reinterpretation of local credit assignment as an approximation problem. More precisely, the authors propose that a rank-1 broadcast can replace the exact compartment-specific field \line . The authors report that shunting inhibition reduces path-gain dispersion, makes exact compartment errors more low-rank, improves LocalCA-to-back-propagation alignment, and improves local-learning performance relative to an additive E/I control.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Significance. The main contribution of the paper is conceptual. It proposes mechanism by which dendritic biophysics could alter credit assignment. Rather than treating inhibition only as a way to suppress neural activity, the paper proposess that conductance-based inhibition changes local input resistance, therefore changes both local synaptic sensitivity and the gain with which errors from distal branches transport toward the soma. This implies that inhibition can select which dendritic compartments receive strong versus weak credit signals. This is an intresting contribution regarding the biological credit assignment problem.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Contribution Type: General: Most submissions will fall into this type.\line Strengths And Weaknesses:\line Strengths\line I find the factorisation of the loss an intresting contribution\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 The implemented experiments aim to distinguish the underlying mechanism by measuring gradient reconstruction, local-to-back-propagation alignment, norm mismatch, path-gain coefficient of variation, error-matrix singular values, inhibitory interventions, morphology dependence, and feedback-bandwidth dependence.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Weaknesses\line Optimal rank-1 approximation is not equivalent to the uniform spatial broadcast used by the algorithm. The approximation assumes scalar broadcast (the rank-1 approximation to have an all one spatial vector), while the experiments test for rank-1 compressibility, which is not the same, because in a general rank-1 approximation one vector is not necessarily uniform, neither can it always be transformed into one.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 The result is established for a directed feedforward conductance tree.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 The more well performing results depend on the empirical 5F modifier, while the theorem-derived 3F rule performs much worse. Thus I would say that the paper does not show (yet) that shunting plus a scalar broadcast are sufficient for local learning. It rather shows that this combination is useful with additional empirically chosen local preconditioning.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Minor\line There is some overlap of text and other objects/arrows in some figures of the paper.\line Please explain why the residual-variance factor \line  should be considered as a confidence measure.\line The abstract mentions abbreviations (LocalCA, 5F etc) that are not resolved before, so the reader has no idea what these mean, without reading the full text.\line Figure 1 caption: "gold-ringed soma" I think with this phrase the authors refer to the schematic illustrating soma with a yellow/gold ring. However, I find the word "gold-ringed" odd, while the sentence as it is structured, does not indicate that the authors refer to the illustration.\line Phrase "synapse banks" sounds odd to me, not sure whether it is often used.\line I would start first with introducing the equation 1 and then writing the paragraph currently in lines 78 - 105 that mentions the scaling of parameters etc. Otherwise the reader encounters objects/variables without having a concrete idea yet how these relate or fit together in your model. Current version first describes how equations behave, and then reports the equations which is uncomfortable to read, because the reader has to skim through the text to find the relations you are referring to.\line Quality: 2: not good\line Clarity: 2: not good\line Significance: 3: good\line Originality: 3: good\line Questions:\line can the authors define over which axes the covariance, variance, path-gain CV, and error-matrix SVD are computed in every figure.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 What is the constrained reconstruction error of the exact compartment-error field using the exact spatial form available to the rank-1 broadcast?\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Would the advantage conferred by shunting inhibition persist for 3F alone after matching activation distributions, gradient norms, and learning-rate schedules between additive and shunting models?\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Can you provide shunting-versus-additive comparisons separately for the 3F, 4F, and 5F rules?\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 The authors already cite previous work introducing models with detailed dendrites where different dendritic compartments receive different teaching signals. can the authors probably point out more clear in what way their proposed mechanism differs from these previous approaches?\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 The proposed framework assumes access to the somatic error for the updates. How could this signal be generated biologically?\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Can you provide a theoretical justification on why inhibitory conductances minimise the effective rank of the error matrix?\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Would active dendritic nonlinearities amplify or diminish your path-gain mechanism? Do you have any intuition, theoretical insight or empirical result?\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Do the path-gain statistics depend on the symmetry/ geometry of the dendritic tree?\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Limitations:\line Largely yes.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 The authors should additionally mention that the low-rank SVD analysis measures whether the error field has an optimal unconstrained rank-1 approximation, while the implemented broadcast is more restricted, since it has a uniform spatial pattern across compartments. The paper should state that low-rank alone does not guarantee compatibility with this particular broadcast.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Rating: 2: Reject: For instance, a paper with technical flaws, weak evaluation, inadequate reproducibility and incompletely addressed ethical considerations.\line Confidence: 3: You are fairly confident in your assessment. It is possible that you did not understand some parts of the submission or that you are unfamiliar with some pieces of related work. Math/other details were not carefully checked.\line Ethical Concerns: NO or VERY MINOR ethics concerns only\line Paper Formatting Concerns:\line no\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Code Of Conduct Acknowledgement: Yes\line Responsible Reviewing Acknowledgement: Yes\par
\pard\sb80\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp40\cf4\par
\pard\sb100\sa60\f0\fs24\b\cf3 AUTHOR RESPONSE\b0\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 Thank you for the careful review and for recognizing the factorization as an interesting contribution. Your two central concerns led to the most informative controls in the paper.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 Bottom line. Exact-gradient reconstruction verifies the factorization below 1.9e-7 relative error. With exact path transport, 3F reaches 97.18 to 97.21%, matching backpropagation at 97.03% and 5F at 97.12 to 97.20%. Exact compartment feedback is also unnecessary in the regular tree: one coordinate shared across each modeled neuron's 13 compartments raises 3F to 97.15% in shunting and 97.14% in additive networks, improving all 15 pairs. Feedback routing, not local eligibility, is the main bottleneck.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 1. Constrained feedback form\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 We agree that an unconstrained rank-1 SVD is not equivalent to a uniform spatial broadcast. We have corrected both the terminology and the analysis.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The implemented `per_soma` alias preserves the soma/core vector only when the dendritic-stage width matches it. Wider stages receive one scalar per example. We now call this operation matched-width/scalar-fallback feedback. It is neither a global scalar at every stage nor one soma coordinate repeated over that neuron's descendants.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The requested constrained calculation confirms why this distinction matters. On dendritic compartments, after one optimal global rescaling, the implemented field captures only 2.3% of exact-error energy in shunting and 0.6% in additive checkpoints. There is no reliable cross-core ordering, so we no longer use unrestricted SVD or pooled field metrics to claim shunting-specific feedback compatibility. The SVD is retained only as a descriptive property of the exact error matrix.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The constructive result is much stronger than the removed rank-1 interpretation. Repeating one soma coordinate over each modeled neuron's 13 compartments raises 3F MNIST accuracy from 90.75% to 97.15% in shunting and from 91.58% to 97.14% in additive networks. The paired gains are 6.40 and 5.56 percentage points, occur in all 15 pairs, and have two-sided signed-rank p=6.1e-5 in both architectures. At these checkpoints, substituting only the diagnostic field raises branch-gradient cosine from 0.007 to 0.667 and from 0.024 to 0.599, again in every pair. Thus a single coordinate per neuron, with ancestry supplying the spatial routing map, recovers almost all of the learning achieved by dense transported error.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 This directly answers the constrained-broadcast question: low rank alone is not sufficient, but a low-dimensional field with the correct neuron-indexed spatial basis is highly effective.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 2. Three-, four-, and five-factor rules\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The exact-transport factorial separates the theorem-derived rule from empirical preconditioning. Across five seeds, 3F reaches 97.21+/-0.14% with a backprop-updated decoder and 97.18+/-0.12% with a locally updated decoder, compared with matched backpropagation at 97.03+/-0.08%. The corresponding 5F values are 97.20+/-0.16% and 97.12+/-0.14%. Therefore, 5F is not required when the error factor in the theorem is supplied accurately.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The neuron-wise experiment gives the biologically restricted intermediate result: 3F reaches 97.15% with one coordinate per modeled neuron rather than an independently specified error at every compartment.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 After matching feedback, decoder, optimizer, schedule, and effective parameter-group rates within the archived shunting cohort, 3F/4F/5F accuracy is 89.90/90.05/91.19% (three seeds, descriptive). The like-for-like 3F-to-5F difference is 1.29 points, not the apparent 30-point deficit from mixing configurations.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 For the requested cross-core control, a current-code 2x2 factorial crossed architecture and explicit initialization policy over 15 paired seeds. Under analytical initialization, shunting and additive 3F are identical at 90.92% (paired p=0.98). Under occupancy calibration, additive is modestly higher, 91.66% versus 90.99%, with an architecture-by-policy interaction. We therefore interpret cross-core 3F accuracy as operating-point-dependent rather than as a universal architecture ranking. We do not have a matched additive 4F/5F factorial and make no claim from an unmatched comparison.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The gradient controls agree. An archived three-pair cohort has cosine 0.160 versus 0.030, while an independent five-seed cohort gives 0.155 versus 0.164. Identity transfer gives higher shunting direction but slightly higher additive accuracy. Learning-rate schedules are identical, and norm-matched one-step updates reduce held-out loss in every seed without a core ordering. Occupancy and identity controls do not fully match forward voltage distributions. Direction therefore depends on activation state, feedback identity, and transfer derivatives, so we make no universal architecture claim.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The 5F residual term is a bounded predictability preconditioner, not statistical confidence. We now name and define it accordingly and separate it from 3F.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 3. What shunting contributes\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The exact theoretical result is a branch-selective credit-gain mechanism. For inhibitory conductance at compartment k,\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 `d log(alpha_n) / d G_k^I = -R_k`\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 for every descendant n whose route passes through k, with no such path effect on unrelated branches. Whether this compresses the field depends on where inhibition is placed; in log-gain form the sufficient condition is `2 Cov(z,beta) > Var(beta)`. We therefore do not claim that inhibition automatically minimizes rank.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 Positive signatures survive the stricter analysis. At N_I=5, path-gain CV is about 80% lower under shunting in all five pairs. Under restricted 5F, shunting is higher on MNIST (91.1 versus 89.4%), Fashion-MNIST (83.8 versus 83.1%), figure-ground MNIST (80.3 versus 78.7%), and compact CIFAR-10 (29.7 versus 25.5%). Exact transport raises shunting CIFAR-10 to 47.2%, close to its 49.5% backprop ceiling, while additive reaches 32.4%. Across one to four dendritic layers, shunting changes from 63.5 to 57.4%, while additive changes from 54.9 to 29.7%; under broadcast noise, shunting is stable through sigma=0.1 while additive reaches chance at sigma=1.0. These establish useful regimes, not universal dominance.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The fixed-state intervention clarifies the mechanism at trained operating points. Removing inhibition only from backward resistance changes distal gain by 1.070x on MNIST and 1.281x in the higher-inhibition noise population, but changes branch cosine by less than 0.002. The diagnostic is sensitive to larger path interventions: setting local resistance to one gives cosine 0.948 with a 5.56x norm change, while omitting parent derivatives gives 0.385. Thus the observed learning effects involve inhibition's combined influence on forward voltage, local eligibility, and path gain. This is a quantitative mechanistic boundary, not evidence that conductance is irrelevant.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 4. Scope, geometry, and relation to prior work\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The exact product is derived for an arbitrary rooted feedforward tree, not only a symmetric tree. Path statistics depend on route depth and branch-specific conductances. In a directed acyclic graph the node error becomes a sum over parent paths; cycles require an adjoint or implicit gradient. All 40 depth-sweep checkpoints retain every nominal stage, with minimum stage-median coupling 0.716, excluding stage collapse as the explanation for the depth result.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 A differentiable active nonlinearity contributes its local derivative to the effective path gain. Identity-transfer and parametric-tanh controls show that the selected nonlinearity is not necessary for task competence, while calcium, spikes, and multi-state channels require temporal eligibility or adjoint extensions.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 Prior dendritic learning models posit apical teaching compartments, burst signals, or local targets. Our contribution is complementary and distinct: we derive the exact credit required by a conductance tree, identify its local and non-local factors, and measure which restricted feedback families recover it. Somatic error is assumed rather than biologically derived; apical, burst, plateau, and neuromodulatory signals are candidate carriers. The neuron-wise result sharpens the biological requirement from one error per compartment to one coordinate shared within a modeled neuron.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 5. Presentation\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The revision introduces the voltage equation before implementation conventions, defines all feedback modes, removes unresolved abbreviations, and rebuilds the figures without overlaps. Covariance is over examples after reducing non-batch coordinates; path-gain CV is over compartments within examples; SVD uses an examples-by-compartments matrix; gradient metrics compare matched parameter vectors. The main argument now follows one chain: exact factorization, feedback approximation, mechanism, learning, and biological predictions.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The resulting claim is both stronger and more precise: dendritic gradients factor exactly into local eligibility and path-transported error; the 3F rule reaches backpropagation when feedback preserves the required structure; neuron-indexed routing captures most of this benefit with one coordinate per neuron; and shunting provides an exact, branch-selective mechanism for regulating credit whose learning benefit is regime-dependent.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 We hope these controls directly resolve the rank-1 and 3F concerns while preserving the conceptual contribution you identified.\par
\pard\sb80\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp40\cf4\par
