\pard\sa60\f1\fs30\b\cf1 Reviewer s2E9\b0\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp40\cf4\par
\pard\sb80\sa50\f0\fs17\b\cf2 ORIGINAL REVIEW\b0\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Official Review of Submission29735 by Reviewer s2E9\line Official Reviewby Reviewer s2E925 Jun 2026, 05:58 (modified: 23 Jul 2026, 12:43)Program Chairs, Senior Area Chairs, Area Chairs, Reviewers Submitted, Authors, Reviewer s2E9Revisions\line Summary:\line The paper tries to solve the fundamental credit assignment problem. In standard backprop, we say that the delta w is proportional to the error and the activation. While the authors say that, in the case of pyramidal neurons, no distinct credit is assigned to each neuron, unlike in standard backpropagation. The paper claims that there is a low-bandwidth global signal rather than local signals, i.e., a credit for each neuron. Authors evaluate whether three components such as tree-structured dendrites, excitatory/inhibitory conductance synapses, and shunting inhibition can reshape the geometry of error propagation. In here, the shunting Inhibition acts as a control mechanism for error transmission in dendritic paths.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Contribution Type: General: Most submissions will fall into this type.\line Strengths And Weaknesses:\line Strengths\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 The shift from developing a new local learning rule to replace backprop to the analysis if a neuron's biophysics can make the backprop easier to approximate is novel.\line The derivation of the exact gradients for dendritic trees and proving that synaptic gradients factorise into a local eligibility term and a non-local compartment error provides a rigorous mathematical framework for local learning.\line The theoretical claims are supported by the right set of experiments, such as gradient reconstruction, alignments, error compressibility, interventions by inhibition and oracle.\line Weakness\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 The scalability of the method isn't shown in the paper due to its limited evaluation on Fashion MNIST, CIFAR-10, and synthetic tasks. Evaluation should be shown on larger datasets, such as CIF100, TinyImagenet, Imagenet-A, or R.\line From equation (4) we understand that the \line  is described as a compartment error, but the theory isn't clear on how the path gain \line  can be learned or estimated.\line The advantages of shunting inhibition aren't theoretically justified. Rather, it's empirically shown in the paper.\line The change of neuron from pyramidal or even if just the structure changes from a single parent, leading to a non-unique path, changing the equations. Generalizability is not shown with respect to different networks or across datasets.\line Quality: 3: good\line Clarity: 3: good\line Significance: 3: good\line Originality: 3: good\line Questions:\line What is the goal of the paper - to bridge the gap between neuroscience and deep learning? In that case, it would be great to understand the biophysical underpinnings of this work, for instance, how inhibitory neurotransmitters mediate shunting inhibition in the classification task? Given that computations in the brain are more precisely represented by Hodgkin-Huxley-like models, and neuronal spikes also are shown to play a role.\line If the goal is to improve deep learning inspired by neuroscience, then please extend your evaluation to STOA datasets like ImageNet and ImageNet-R. A comparison with STOA performance is also necessary.\line A significant amount of such learning algorithm variants exists in the literature, such as FF, PEPITA, SPELA, Trifecta, NoProp, LLS to name a few. Please thoroughly compare your work with similar works.\line It's not clear why we should go for shunting inhibition from the present manuscript contents. Please compare and report the memory, wall-clock time, and energy estimates for your work with STOA models, in addition to classification accuracy.\line How would you extend this design to CNNs or transformers?\line Limitations:\line Yes\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Rating: 3: Borderline reject: Technically solid paper where reasons to reject, e.g., limited evaluation, outweigh reasons to accept, e.g., good evaluation. Please use sparingly.\line Confidence: 4: You are confident in your assessment, but not absolutely certain. It is unlikely, but not impossible, that you did not understand some parts of the submission or that you are unfamiliar with some pieces of related work.\line Ethical Concerns: NO or VERY MINOR ethics concerns only\line Paper Formatting Concerns:\line None\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 [Minor] I would prefer to read the experimental results in the main paper rather than in the appendix.\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\sl220\slmult1\f0\fs17\cf2 Code Of Conduct Acknowledgement: Yes\line Responsible Reviewing Acknowledgement: Yes\par
\pard\sb80\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp40\cf4\par
\pard\sb100\sa60\f0\fs24\b\cf3 AUTHOR RESPONSE\b0\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 Thank you for recognizing the novelty of asking whether neuronal biophysics can make exact credit easier to approximate. We agree that the goal and the evidence for practical relevance should be stated directly.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 Bottom line. This is a mechanism-first NeuroAI paper, not a claim of ImageNet-scale efficiency. It derives the exact credit equation of a conductance tree, verifies it numerically to relative error below 1.9e-7, and identifies feedback routing as the limiting component. With exact transported errors, the theorem-derived 3F rule reaches 97.18 to 97.21% on MNIST, matching backpropagation at 97.03%. With only one teaching coordinate shared across the 13 compartments of each modeled neuron, 3F reaches 97.15% in shunting and 97.14% in additive networks. On the harder compact CIFAR-10 control, exact transport raises shunting LocalCA from 29.7% to 47.2%, close to the matched 49.5% backpropagation ceiling. These are quantitative tests of the proposed credit mechanism.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 1. Goal and novelty\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The paper makes a direct bridge from a biophysical component to a learning computation:\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 1. derive the exact gradient of a conductance-based dendritic tree;\line 2. separate it into synapse-local eligibility and path-transported compartment error;\line 3. measure how E/I conductance, shunting, and branching transform that error;\line 4. test which restricted feedback fields preserve enough information for learning.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 FF, PEPITA, SPELA, Trifecta, NoProp, and LLS primarily design layer-local or forward-only objectives. Our work instead starts from the exact conductance-tree gradient and asks which factors are local and how neuronal structure changes the required teaching signal. A comparison table distinguishes feedback source, within-neuron biophysics, objective, and relation to exact credit.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 For neuroscience, the framework predicts descendant-selective plasticity changes after focal shunting, set by input resistance and path geometry, and can be applied to reconstructed morphologies. For AI, it identifies neuron-indexed and path-aware feedback as structure to preserve at scale. The code implements matched cores, E/I and morphology interventions, six feedback families, and exact-gradient checks.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 2. What is learned, and what shunting controls\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The path gain alpha_n is not a separately learned parameter. It is the instantaneous derivative `dV_soma/dV_n`, determined by the current branch-to-parent conductances, input resistances, and local transfer derivatives. On a rooted tree it is the product of these local gains along the unique route. Backpropagation and the transported-error analysis compute it from the current state; practical LocalCA deliberately does not, allowing us to measure the cost of restricted feedback.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 Shunting has an exact theoretical role. Increasing inhibitory conductance at compartment k changes every descendant path gain according to\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 `d log(alpha_n) / d G_k^I = -R_k`,\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 with no corresponding path effect on unrelated branches. This gives a biologically grounded, compartment-local control over both synaptic eligibility and descendant credit gain. It does not imply that every placement of inhibition helps; the benefit depends on the affected route and task.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The experiments provide several positive signatures. At N_I=5, conductance-stage path-gain CV is about 80% lower under shunting, with the same ordering in all five pairs and at every nonzero inhibitory count. Under restricted 5F feedback, shunting exceeds additive on MNIST (91.1% versus 89.4%), Fashion-MNIST (83.8% versus 83.1%), figure-ground MNIST (80.3% versus 78.7%), and compact CIFAR-10 (29.7% versus 25.5%). In the depth stress test, shunting changes from 63.5% to 57.4% across one to four dendritic layers, while additive changes from 54.9% to 29.7%. Under broadcast noise, shunting is stable through sigma=0.1, whereas additive reaches chance at sigma=1.0. These results show why shunting is worth studying: it provides a selective conductance mechanism and is useful when paths are deep, feedback is noisy, or the task is inhibition-sensitive.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 A 15-seed architecture-by-initialization factorial gives equal 3F accuracy under analytical initialization, 90.92% in both cores, and a modest additive advantage under occupancy calibration. Backward-only removal changes distal gain by 1.070x on MNIST and 1.281x in the higher-inhibition noise population, but gradient cosine by less than 0.002. Thus the learning effects involve forward voltage, local eligibility, and path gain together, not isolated backward attenuation.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 3. Three-factor learning and feedback routing\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The two strongest controls show that 3F is not the limiting factor.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 First, in a five-seed factorial with exact path-transported errors, 3F reaches 97.21+/-0.14% with a backprop-updated decoder and 97.18+/-0.12% with a locally updated decoder. The corresponding 5F values are 97.20+/-0.16% and 97.12+/-0.14%, and matched backpropagation is 97.03+/-0.08%. Therefore, empirical 5F preconditioning is unnecessary when the theorem's error factor is supplied accurately.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 Second, dense compartment errors are not necessary in the regular tree. Replacing scalar fallback with one soma-error coordinate repeated over each modeled neuron's 13 compartments raises 3F accuracy from 90.75% to 97.15% in shunting and from 91.58% to 97.14% in additive networks. The gains of 6.40 and 5.56 points occur in all 15 pairs, with signed-rank p=6.1e-5. The corresponding branch-gradient cosine increases from 0.007 to 0.667 and from 0.024 to 0.599. This result turns the feedback question into a constructive design principle: preserve neuron identity and use the tree as a routing map.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 We corrected the feedback terminology: the original alias preserves the soma vector at a width-matched stage and otherwise uses a scalar. It is not ancestry-shared feedback, and unconstrained rank-1 SVD does not test a uniform broadcast. The revised analysis separates intrinsic geometry from implemented-field compatibility.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 4. Scale and benchmark evidence\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 We agree that scale is important, but the current CIFAR-10 ladder already tests the mechanism on a harder input distribution. Under the same compact passive architecture, restricted shunting LocalCA reaches 29.7+/-1.3%, rank-4 feedback reaches 35.0+/-1.0%, exact transported error reaches 47.2+/-0.6%, and matched shunting backpropagation reaches 49.5+/-0.4%. The 17.5-point recovery from restricted to transported feedback, reaching within 2.3 points of the architecture's ceiling, isolates credit quality rather than forward capacity. Additive exact transport reaches 32.4+/-1.5%, providing an additional architecture control.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 We added a directly implementable DFA reference on matched MNIST models. DFA reaches 66.1% in shunting, 62.2% in additive, and 51.8% in a point MLP; their respective gaps to matched backpropagation are 24.9, 27.6, and 39.5 points. This is not a comprehensive leaderboard, but it positions the mechanism beside a standard broadcast alternative without changing the within-unit question.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The next test is to insert the unit into a competitive CNN or transformer and compare feedback modes under matched augmentation and compute. In CNNs, patches provide local eligibility and shared parameters sum over positions; in transformers, dendritic units can replace feed-forward or value/output projections. Credit between blocks remains separate.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 5. Compute, memory, and energy\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 With the same MNIST model, batch size, hooks, evaluation, and 180 epochs, LocalCA takes 190 s versus 125 s for backpropagation. Peak allocated memory is 1.70 GiB for both (2.03 versus 1.97 GiB reserved). The research implementation is feasible but not yet an efficiency method. Hardware energy was not measured.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 6. Biological scope and generality\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The model is a rooted conductance tree, not a complete pyramidal-cell circuit. With multiple parents, local eligibility still factorizes from node error, but the error sums over parent paths. Recurrence requires an adjoint; Hodgkin-Huxley channels, spikes, calcium, and interneurons add temporal state and eligibility traces and may change credit substantially.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The classification labels do not stand for neurotransmitters. Inhibitory neurotransmission is represented by input-driven conductance changing local input resistance, forward voltage sensitivity, and path gain. Classification and synthetic tasks are controlled probes of the resulting learning geometry. A complete biological implementation also requires a source of neuron-indexed teaching signals; apical, burst, plateau, and neuromodulatory signals are candidates rather than established mechanisms here.\par
\pard\sb0\sa140\sl280\slmult1\f0\fs23\cf3 The revised presentation brings the factorization, feedback distinction, principal quantitative controls, biological predictions, and limitations into the main argument. The resulting contribution is a new mechanistic framework with a validated local rule, an identified feedback bottleneck, regime-specific evidence for shunting, and a concrete path to reconstructed-neuron and larger-backbone tests.\par
\pard\sb80\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp40\cf4\par
